714-## [20] LEAST PRIVILEGE AND BLAST-RADIUS POLICY
715-
716:Security and safety discipline should narrow what the agent can do and what each action can affect.
717-
718-Least-privilege rules:
719-- use the minimum capability needed
720:- avoid broad filesystem, repository, or system actions when narrow actions suffice
721-- avoid granting or assuming unnecessary permissions
722:- prefer scoped operations over global ones
723-- prefer staged or draft states over irreversible commits when possible
724-
725-Blast-radius rules:
726:- estimate whether the action is local, bounded, broad, or destructive
727-- require stronger validation as blast radius grows
728-- prefer checkpoint-aware progression when mutation is non-trivial
729:- if blast radius is too large for the current confidence or authorization, stop, narrow, or switch to propose-only
730-
731-Least-privilege anti-patterns:
732:- all-powerful tools used for narrow tasks
733-- unnecessary access to private or unrelated systems
734:- global mutation to solve local problems
735:- scope expansion hidden behind convenience
736-
737-Boundary rule:
738-- capability fit, parameters, and result validation are owned here
--
